      "timelineId": "tale-of-two-cities-timeline-main",
      "number": 45,
      "title": "Book the Third — The Track of a Storm: The Footsteps Die Out For Ever",
      "synopsis": "In the third tumbril, a young prisoner recognizes that Carton has taken another man’s place and asks to hold his hand. At the guillotine, Carton imagines the family safe, Lucie naming a son for him, and violence exhausting itself before renewal.",
      "notes": "",
